/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Daniel chapters 1-5
   Questions authored from the KJV chapter text (fetched from bible-api.com).
   Per spec: verse:"" stays empty everywhere; correct answer is always options[0]. */
VG.registerBibleChapters("daniel", [
{n:1, name:"Faith at the King's Table", seal:{ref:"Daniel 1:8",verse:"But Daniel purposed in his heart that he would not defile himself with the portion of the king’s meat, nor with the wine which he drank: therefore he requested of the prince of the eunuchs that he might not defile himself."}, facts:["Did you know the four asked for pulse, simple vegetables, and water for ten days, and finished the trial looking fairer and fatter than the youths who ate the king's rich food (Daniel 1:15)?","Did you know Daniel's stand began in his heart before it reached his mouth? Scripture says he 'purposed in his heart' not to defile himself, the decision before the diet (Daniel 1:8).","Did you know Daniel served in Babylon from the reign of Nebuchadnezzar all the way to the first year of Cyrus, a career of faithfulness spanning the whole captivity (Daniel 1:21)?"], questions:[
{q:"When did Nebuchadnezzar come to Jerusalem and besiege it?", options:["In the third year of the reign of Jehoiakim king of Judah","In the first year of the reign of Zedekiah","In the tenth year of Jehoiakim's reign","In the second year of Nebuchadnezzar's own reign"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:1",verse:"In the third year of the reign of Jehoiakim king of Judah came Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon unto Jerusalem, and besieged it.", insight:"God's story unfolds inside dated history; the siege was real, and so was His purpose in it."},
{q:"What did the Lord give into Nebuchadnezzar's hand?", options:["Jehoiakim king of Judah, with part of the vessels of the house of God","The ark of the covenant and all the temple gold","The priests of Judah and their families","The city walls and gates of Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:2",verse:"And the Lord gave Jehoiakim king of Judah into his hand, with part of the vessels of the house of God: which he carried into the land of Shinar to the house of his god; and he brought the vessels into the treasure house of his god.", insight:"Even in judgment God stays in charge; nothing was taken that He had not given."},
{q:"Who was the master of the king's eunuchs?", options:["Ashpenaz","Arioch","Melzar","Belteshazzar"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:3",verse:"And the king spake unto Ashpenaz the master of his eunuchs, that he should bring certain of the children of Israel, and of the king’s seed, and of the princes;", insight:"God places His people under specific keepers; even a Babylonian official can become an instrument of mercy."},
{q:"What kind of young men did the king order to be brought?", options:["Children with no blemish, well favoured, and skilled in all wisdom","Only the sons of the priests","Only trained soldiers","Only the sons of farmers"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:4",verse:"Children in whom was no blemish, but well favoured, and skilful in all wisdom, and cunning in knowledge, and understanding science, and such as had ability in them to stand in the king’s palace, and whom they might teach the learning and the tongue of the Chaldeans.", insight:"Babylon wanted the best of Judah's youth; God meant to keep the best for Himself."},
{q:"What daily provision did the king appoint for them?", options:["The king's meat, and the wine which he drank","Bread and oil from the royal stores","Pulse and water only","Fruit and honey cakes"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:5",verse:"And the king appointed them a daily provision of the king’s meat, and of the wine which he drank: so nourishing them three years, that at the end thereof they might stand before the king.", insight:"The king's table was a test disguised as a gift; Daniel saw through it."},
{q:"For how many years were they to be nourished before standing before the king?", options:["Three years","One year","Seven years","Ten years"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:5",verse:"And the king appointed them a daily provision of the king’s meat, and of the wine which he drank: so nourishing them three years, that at the end thereof they might stand before the king.", insight:"Three years of quiet training; God forms His servants long before He shows them."},
{q:"Which four young men of Judah are named in this chapter?", options:["Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah","Jeremiah, Ezekiel, Baruch, and Seraiah","Shadrach, Meshach, Abednego, and Daniel","Zerubbabel, Joshua, Haggai, and Zechariah"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:6",verse:"Now among these were of the children of Judah, Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah:", insight:"Four names history remembers; faithfulness made them famous, not Babylon."},
{q:"What Babylonian name was given to Daniel?", options:["Belteshazzar","Shadrach","Meshach","Abednego"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:7",verse:"Unto whom the prince of the eunuchs gave names: for he gave unto Daniel the name of Belteshazzar; and to Hananiah, of Shadrach; and to Mishael, of Meshach; and to Azariah, of Abed-nego.", insight:"Babylon renamed the boy, but it could not rename his heart; Daniel stayed Daniel inside."},
{q:"Why would Daniel not eat the king's meat or drink his wine?", options:["He purposed in his heart that he would not defile himself","He disliked the taste of foreign food","He was keeping a forty day fast","The prince of the eunuchs had forbidden it"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:8",verse:"But Daniel purposed in his heart that he would not defile himself with the portion of the king’s meat, nor with the wine which he drank: therefore he requested of the prince of the eunuchs that he might not defile himself.", insight:"The battle was won in the heart before it reached the table; decide early, and the moment decides itself."},
{q:"What had God brought Daniel into with the prince of the eunuchs?", options:["Favour and tender love","Fear and suspicion","Open conflict","Cold indifference"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:9",verse:"Now God had brought Daniel into favour and tender love with the prince of the eunuchs.", insight:"Conviction earns favor even from unlikely hearts; God softens the very officials He placed over you."},
{q:"What did the prince of the eunuchs fear?", options:["That the king would see their faces worse liking, and he would lose his head","That Daniel would report him to the king","That the Chaldeans would laugh at him","That his wages would be cut"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:10",verse:"And the prince of the eunuchs said unto Daniel, I fear my lord the king, who hath appointed your meat and your drink: for why should he see your faces worse liking than the children which are of your sort? then shall ye make me endanger my head to the king.", insight:"His fear was real, and Daniel honored it; courage that listens finds a way forward."},
{q:"To whom did Daniel propose the ten day test?", options:["Melzar, who was set over the four","Ashpenaz, the master of the eunuchs","Arioch, the captain of the guard","Nebuchadnezzar himself"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:11",verse:"Then said Daniel to Melzar, whom the prince of the eunuchs had set over Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah,", insight:"Daniel worked through the right channels; faith does not despise order."},
{q:"What did Daniel ask to eat and drink for ten days?", options:["Pulse to eat, and water to drink","The king's meat and wine","Bread and oil","Nothing at all"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:12",verse:"Prove thy servants, I beseech thee, ten days; and let them give us pulse to eat, and water to drink.", insight:"A humble menu, offered in faith; God does not need rich food to make His servants flourish."},
{q:"How long did Melzar prove them?", options:["Ten days","Three days","Seven days","Forty days"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:14",verse:"So he consented to them in this matter, and proved them ten days.", insight:"Ten days of trust; small trials prove great convictions."},
{q:"What did their countenances look like at the end of the ten days?", options:["Fairer and fatter in flesh than all who ate the king's meat","Pale and thin from hunger","Exactly as before","Worse liking than the others"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:15",verse:"And at the end of ten days their countenances appeared fairer and fatter in flesh than all the children which did eat the portion of the king’s meat.", insight:"Obedience showed on their faces; holiness has a look, and the world can see it."},
{q:"What did Melzar then take away, and what did he give instead?", options:["He took the portion of their meat and wine, and gave them pulse","He took their Babylonian names and gave Hebrew ones","He took their books and gave them scrolls","He took their freedom and gave them chains"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:16",verse:"Thus Melzar took away the portion of their meat, and the wine that they should drink; and gave them pulse.", insight:"The trial became the diet; what God blesses stays on the table."},
{q:"What did God give to these four children?", options:["Knowledge and skill in all learning and wisdom","Gold and silver from the treasury","Houses in the city of Babylon","Command over the Chaldeans"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:17",verse:"As for these four children, God gave them knowledge and skill in all learning and wisdom: and Daniel had understanding in all visions and dreams.", insight:"God gave what Babylon's schools could not; true wisdom comes from above, not from the curriculum."},
{q:"What special understanding did Daniel have?", options:["Understanding in all visions and dreams","The strength of ten men","Knowledge of healing herbs","Skill with the sword"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:17",verse:"As for these four children, God gave them knowledge and skill in all learning and wisdom: and Daniel had understanding in all visions and dreams.", insight:"God gave Daniel eyes for the night visions; He equips each servant for the work ahead."},
{q:"How did the four compare with the magicians and astrologers of Babylon?", options:["The king found them ten times better","They were twice as good","They were about equal","They were found worse"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:20",verse:"And in all matters of wisdom and understanding, that the king enquired of them, he found them ten times better than all the magicians and astrologers that were in all his realm.", insight:"Ten times better; excellence is a quiet witness that needs no boasting."},
{q:"How long did Daniel continue in Babylon?", options:["Even unto the first year of king Cyrus","Only until the third year","Until he fled to Egypt","For seven years exactly"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 1:21",verse:"And Daniel continued even unto the first year of king Cyrus.", insight:"From Nebuchadnezzar to Cyrus, through every regime change; faithfulness outlasts empires."}
]},
{n:2, name:"The Forgotten Dream", seal:{ref:"Daniel 2:28",verse:"But there is a God in heaven that revealeth secrets, and maketh known to the king Nebuchadnezzar what shall be in the latter days. Thy dream, and the visions of thy head upon thy bed, are these;"}, facts:["Did you know Daniel and his three friends held a prayer meeting before the night vision came? They 'desired mercies of the God of heaven,' and heaven answered the same night (Daniel 2:18).","Did you know the Chaldeans confessed that only 'the gods, whose dwelling is not with flesh' could reveal the dream, which set up Daniel's answer perfectly: 'there is a God in heaven that revealeth secrets' (Daniel 2:11).","Did you know the stone cut out without hands became a great mountain filling the whole earth, the Bible's sweeping picture of God's everlasting kingdom (Daniel 2:35)?"], questions:[
{q:"In which year of his reign did Nebuchadnezzar dream his troubling dreams?", options:["In the second year","In the first year","In the seventh year","In the tenth year"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:1",verse:"And in the second year of the reign of Nebuchadnezzar Nebuchadnezzar dreamed dreams, wherewith his spirit was troubled, and his sleep brake from him.", insight:"The second year of his reign; God disturbed the most powerful man on earth with a dream he could not keep."},
{q:"How did the dreams affect the king?", options:["His spirit was troubled, and his sleep brake from him","He laughed and forgot them by morning","He wrote them down calmly","He told them to his wives"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:1",verse:"And in the second year of the reign of Nebuchadnezzar Nebuchadnezzar dreamed dreams, wherewith his spirit was troubled, and his sleep brake from him.", insight:"Troubled spirit, broken sleep; God can unsettle a throne with a single night."},
{q:"Whom did the king command to call to show him the dream?", options:["The magicians, the astrologers, the sorcerers, and the Chaldeans","Only the priests of Bel","His army captains","The elders of Judah"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:2",verse:"Then the king commanded to call the magicians, and the astrologers, and the sorcerers, and the Chaldeans, for to shew the king his dreams. So they came and stood before the king.", insight:"He summoned every wise man in Babylon; human wisdom gathered in full will still come up empty without God."},
{q:"In what language did the Chaldeans answer the king?", options:["In Syriack","In Hebrew","In the tongue of the Medes","In Egyptian"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:4",verse:"Then spake the Chaldeans to the king in Syriack, O king, live for ever: tell thy servants the dream, and we will shew the interpretation.", insight:"They answered politely in the court language, but politeness could not supply what the king demanded."},
{q:"What did the king say about the dream itself?", options:["The thing is gone from me","I remember every detail","It was written on the wall","My servants told it to me"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:5",verse:"The king answered and said to the Chaldeans, The thing is gone from me: if ye will not make known unto me the dream, with the interpretation thereof, ye shall be cut in pieces, and your houses shall be made a dunghill.", insight:"The dream was gone, but the demand stood; God arranged the forgetting to expose the frauds."},
{q:"What punishment did the king threaten if they failed?", options:["They would be cut in pieces, and their houses made a dunghill","They would be exiled to Egypt","They would lose their wages","They would serve in the palace kitchens"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:5",verse:"The king answered and said to the Chaldeans, The thing is gone from me: if ye will not make known unto me the dream, with the interpretation thereof, ye shall be cut in pieces, and your houses shall be made a dunghill.", insight:"Tyrants threaten what they cannot control; fear is a poor foundation for truth."},
{q:"What did the Chaldeans admit no king had ever asked?", options:["Such a thing of any magician, or astrologer, or Chaldean","For gold from the treasury","For a new law","For a son to rule"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:10",verse:"The Chaldeans answered before the king, and said, There is not a man upon the earth that can shew the king’s matter: therefore there is no king, lord, nor ruler, that asked such things at any magician, or astrologer, or Chaldean.", insight:"They were right; no man on earth could do it. That was exactly the point."},
{q:"In his anger, what did the king command?", options:["To destroy all the wise men of Babylon","To burn the palace","To close the temples","To double the guards"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:12",verse:"For this cause the king was angry and very furious, and commanded to destroy all the wise men of Babylon.", insight:"Fury is the tyrant's answer to failure; Daniel's calm would soon stand in sharp contrast."},
{q:"Who was the captain of the king's guard sent to slay the wise men?", options:["Arioch","Ashpenaz","Melzar","Belteshazzar"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:14",verse:"Then Daniel answered with counsel and wisdom to Arioch the captain of the king’s guard, which was gone forth to slay the wise men of Babylon:", insight:"Arioch came with a sword, but Daniel met him with counsel and wisdom; calm disarms haste."},
{q:"What did Daniel ask of the king?", options:["That he would give him time to show the interpretation","For gold and silver","For the lives of the Chaldeans only","To be made a prince"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:16",verse:"Then Daniel went in, and desired of the king that he would give him time, and that he would shew the king the interpretation.", insight:"He asked for time, not for safety; faith requests a window, not a guarantee."},
{q:"To whom did Daniel make the matter known?", options:["Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah, his companions","The magicians of Babylon","The king's counsellors","The elders of Judah"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:17",verse:"Then Daniel went to his house, and made the thing known to Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah, his companions:", insight:"He carried the crisis to his friends, not his fears; prayer is better shared."},
{q:"What did the four desire of the God of heaven?", options:["Mercies concerning this secret, that they should not perish","Riches and honour","The king's favour","A sign in the heavens"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:18",verse:"That they would desire mercies of the God of heaven concerning this secret; that Daniel and his fellows should not perish with the rest of the wise men of Babylon.", insight:"They asked for mercies, not miracles on demand; humble prayer opens heaven's secrets."},
{q:"How was the secret revealed to Daniel?", options:["In a night vision","By a voice from the temple","In a scroll from the king","Through the astrologers"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:19",verse:"Then was the secret revealed unto Daniel in a night vision. Then Daniel blessed the God of heaven.", insight:"God answered in the night, while the city slept; He still speaks when we are quiet enough to hear."},
{q:"What did Daniel say God does with kings?", options:["He removeth kings, and setteth up kings","He forgets the kings of the earth","He serves the greatest kings","He fears no king"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:21",verse:"And he changeth the times and the seasons: he removeth kings, and setteth up kings: he giveth wisdom unto the wise, and knowledge to them that know understanding:", insight:"Kings rise and fall at His word; the throne of heaven never changes hands."},
{q:"What did Daniel declare before the king about God?", options:["There is a God in heaven that revealeth secrets","There is no God in heaven","The gods of Babylon are greater","The king himself is a god"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:28",verse:"But there is a God in heaven that revealeth secrets, and maketh known to the king Nebuchadnezzar what shall be in the latter days. Thy dream, and the visions of thy head upon thy bed, are these;", insight:"The sentence that answers every impossible demand; heaven holds what earth cannot find."},
{q:"Of what were the image's head, breast, and arms made?", options:["The head of fine gold, the breast and arms of silver","The head of silver, the breast of gold","The head of brass, the arms of iron","The head of clay, the breast of brass"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:32",verse:"This image’s head was of fine gold, his breast and his arms of silver, his belly and his thighs of brass,", insight:"Gold gives way to silver; every empire is a downgrade from the one before."},
{q:"What smote the image upon its feet of iron and clay?", options:["A stone cut out without hands","A sword from heaven","A flood of waters","A mighty wind"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:34",verse:"Thou sawest till that a stone was cut out without hands, which smote the image upon his feet that were of iron and clay, and brake them to pieces.", insight:"No human hand shaped the stone; God's kingdom comes by His power, not man's."},
{q:"What became of the stone that smote the image?", options:["It became a great mountain, and filled the whole earth","It vanished into the sea","It crumbled to dust","It was carried to Babylon"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:35",verse:"Then was the iron, the clay, the brass, the silver, and the gold, broken to pieces together, and became like the chaff of the summer threshingfloors; and the wind carried them away, that no place was found for them: and the stone that smote the image became a great mountain, and filled the whole earth.", insight:"A stone becomes a mountain filling the earth; small beginnings, endless ending."},
{q:"What did 'Thou art this head of gold' mean?", options:["Nebuchadnezzar himself was the golden head of the image","Daniel was the head","The temple was the head","Babylon would fall that night"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:38",verse:"And wheresoever the children of men dwell, the beasts of the field and the fowls of the heaven hath he given into thine hand, and hath made thee ruler over them all. Thou art this head of gold.", insight:"The king was the head of gold, glorious and doomed; God names empires, and their expiry dates."},
{q:"What kingdom did Daniel say the God of heaven would set up?", options:["A kingdom which shall never be destroyed, and shall stand for ever","A kingdom of gold in Babylon","A kingdom lasting forty years","A kingdom of the Chaldeans"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 2:44",verse:"And in the days of these kings shall the God of heaven set up a kingdom, which shall never be destroyed: and the kingdom shall not be left to other people, but it shall break in pieces and consume all these kingdoms, and it shall stand for ever.", insight:"Every kingdom of men ends; His stands forever. Build your hope on the unshakable one."}
]},
{n:3, name:"The Fiery Furnace", seal:{ref:"Daniel 3:18",verse:"But if not, be it known unto thee, O king, that we will not serve thy gods, nor worship the golden image which thou hast set up."}, facts:["Did you know the king named six instruments, the cornet, flute, harp, sackbut, psaltery, and dulcimer, and commanded the whole empire to worship at their sound (Daniel 3:5)?","Did you know the furnace was heated seven times hotter than usual, and its flames killed the king's own mighty men before the three even touched the fire (Daniel 3:22)?","Did you know Nebuchadnezzar himself said the fourth figure in the fire was 'like the Son of God' (Daniel 3:25)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did Nebuchadnezzar the king make?", options:["An image of gold","A temple of silver","A palace of brass","A statue of clay"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:1",verse:"Nebuchadnezzar the king made an image of gold, whose height was threescore cubits, and the breadth thereof six cubits: he set it up in the plain of Dura, in the province of Babylon.", insight:"An image of gold, all gold; pride loves to gild itself."},
{q:"How large was the image?", options:["Threescore cubits high, and six cubits broad","Ten cubits high and ten broad","A hundred cubits high","Twenty cubits all around"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:1",verse:"Nebuchadnezzar the king made an image of gold, whose height was threescore cubits, and the breadth thereof six cubits: he set it up in the plain of Dura, in the province of Babylon.", insight:"Ninety feet of gold; men build big when they want worship."},
{q:"What did Nebuchadnezzar call the three men from the furnace mouth?", options:["Ye servants of the most high God, come forth, and come hither","Ye rebels of Judah, come out and be judged","Ye wise men of Babylon, come and be honoured","Ye prisoners of the king, come and be pardoned"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:26",verse:"Then Nebuchadnezzar came near to the mouth of the burning fiery furnace, and spake, and said, Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego, ye servants of the most high God, come forth, and come hither. Then Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego, came forth of the midst of the fire.", insight:"Servants of the most high God; the king who demanded worship now named the God he had defied."},
{q:"Who was gathered for the dedication of the image?", options:["The princes, governors, captains, judges, treasurers, counsellors, sheriffs, and all rulers of the provinces","Only the priests of Bel","The army of Babylon alone","The elders of Judah"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:2",verse:"Then Nebuchadnezzar the king sent to gather together the princes, the governors, and the captains, the judges, the treasurers, the counsellors, the sheriffs, and all the rulers of the provinces, to come to the dedication of the image which Nebuchadnezzar the king had set up.", insight:"Every rank of power was summoned; when the world demands worship, it brings its officials."},
{q:"At the sound of what were all to fall down and worship?", options:["The cornet, flute, harp, sackbut, psaltery, dulcimer, and all kinds of musick","A single trumpet","The drums of war","The voice of the herald"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:5",verse:"That at what time ye hear the sound of the cornet, flute, harp, sackbut, psaltery, dulcimer, and all kinds of musick, ye fall down and worship the golden image that Nebuchadnezzar the king hath set up:", insight:"Music as a signal for idolatry; the world still uses beautiful sounds to summon false worship."},
{q:"What was the penalty for not worshipping?", options:["Being cast the same hour into the midst of a burning fiery furnace","Forty lashes","Exile from Babylon","A heavy fine of gold"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:6",verse:"And whoso falleth not down and worshippeth shall the same hour be cast into the midst of a burning fiery furnace.", insight:"Worship or burn; coercion has always been the idol's favorite argument."},
{q:"What did all the people do when they heard the music?", options:["They fell down and worshipped the golden image","They covered their ears","They fled the plain","They sang to the Lord"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:7",verse:"Therefore at that time, when all the people heard the sound of the cornet, flute, harp, sackbut, psaltery, and all kinds of musick, all the people, the nations, and the languages, fell down and worshipped the golden image that Nebuchadnezzar the king had set up.", insight:"Everyone bowed; the crowd always bows. The three who stood are the story."},
{q:"Who accused the Jews before the king?", options:["Certain Chaldeans","The princes of Judah","The king's own sons","The priests of Bel"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:8",verse:"Wherefore at that time certain Chaldeans came near, and accused the Jews.", insight:"Envy watches the faithful; obedience in others exposes compromise in us."},
{q:"What did the accusers say of Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego?", options:["They serve not thy gods, nor worship the golden image","They steal from the treasury","They plot against the king","They refuse to pay tribute"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:12",verse:"There are certain Jews whom thou hast set over the affairs of the province of Babylon, Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego; these men, O king, have not regarded thee: they serve not thy gods, nor worship the golden image which thou hast set up.", insight:"The charge was true, and they were glad of it; a good conscience turns accusation into testimony."},
{q:"How did Nebuchadnezzar respond to the report?", options:["In his rage and fury he commanded to bring them","He laughed and dismissed it","He sent them gifts","He forgot the matter"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:13",verse:"Then Nebuchadnezzar in his rage and fury commanded to bring Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego. Then they brought these men before the king.", insight:"Rage and fury; threatened pride always shouts first."},
{q:"What did the king ask the three men?", options:["Do not ye serve my gods, nor worship the golden image which I have set up?","Will ye not pay your taxes?","Why have ye left the province?","Who taught you rebellion?"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:14",verse:"Nebuchadnezzar spake and said unto them, Is it true, O Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego, do not ye serve my gods, nor worship the golden image which I have set up?", insight:"He gave them a chance to deny the charge; they would not take it."},
{q:"What second chance did the king offer them?", options:["If ready at the music to worship, well; if not, the same hour into the furnace","A month to think it over","Exile instead of death","A private worship in the palace"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:15",verse:"Now if ye be ready that at what time ye hear the sound of the cornet, flute, harp, sackbut, psaltery, and dulcimer, and all kinds of musick, ye fall down and worship the image which I have made; well: but if ye worship not, ye shall be cast the same hour into the midst of a burning fiery furnace; and who is that God that shall deliver you out of my hands?", insight:"One more song, one more chance to bow; grace periods from tyrants are just delayed threats."},
{q:"What bold question did the king ask them?", options:["Who is that God that shall deliver you out of my hands?","Who is your father in Judah?","Who told you to disobey?","Who shall rule after me?"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:15",verse:"Now if ye be ready that at what time ye hear the sound of the cornet, flute, harp, sackbut, psaltery, and dulcimer, and all kinds of musick, ye fall down and worship the image which I have made; well: but if ye worship not, ye shall be cast the same hour into the midst of a burning fiery furnace; and who is that God that shall deliver you out of my hands?", insight:"He mocked the very idea of deliverance; heaven was listening, and heaven would answer."},
{q:"What did the three answer about their God?", options:["Our God whom we serve is able to deliver us from the burning fiery furnace","Our God is too weak to help us","We have no God to call upon","The gods of Babylon will save us"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:17",verse:"If it be so, our God whom we serve is able to deliver us from the burning fiery furnace, and he will deliver us out of thine hand, O king.", insight:"Able to deliver; they anchored their courage in God's ability, not their odds."},
{q:"What did they add with 'But if not'?", options:["We will not serve thy gods, nor worship the golden image","We will worship when we are older","We will serve in secret","We will flee to Judah"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:18",verse:"But if not, be it known unto thee, O king, that we will not serve thy gods, nor worship the golden image which thou hast set up.", insight:"But if not; faith that obeys whether or not it is rescued is the strongest faith of all."},
{q:"How hot did the king command the furnace to be heated?", options:["One seven times more than it was wont to be heated","Twice as hot as usual","Three times hotter","Ten times hotter"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:19",verse:"Then was Nebuchadnezzar full of fury, and the form of his visage was changed against Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego: therefore he spake, and commanded that they should heat the furnace one seven times more than it was wont to be heated.", insight:"Seven times hotter; fury overcompensates, but fire cannot outburn the presence of God."},
{q:"Who bound Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego?", options:["The most mighty men of the king's army","The Chaldean accusers","The palace servants","Their own friends"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:20",verse:"And he commanded the most mighty men that were in his army to bind Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego, and to cast them into the burning fiery furnace.", insight:"The strongest men in Babylon tied them; strength bound them, but Someone greater would loose them."},
{q:"What happened to the mighty men who cast them in?", options:["The flame of the fire slew them","They were promoted","They fell asleep","They converted on the spot"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:22",verse:"Therefore because the king’s commandment was urgent, and the furnace exceeding hot, the flame of the fire slew those men that took up Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego.", insight:"The fire meant for the faithful killed the executioners; God turns the persecutor's weapon on itself."},
{q:"What did the astonished king see in the fire?", options:["Four men loose, walking in the midst of the fire, with no hurt","Three men turned to ashes","The furnace gone cold","An empty furnace"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:25",verse:"He answered and said, Lo, I see four men loose, walking in the midst of the fire, and they have no hurt; and the form of the fourth is like the Son of God.", insight:"He counted three bound and saw four walking free; God joins His people in the fire."},
{q:"What did the officials find when the three came out?", options:["No hurt, no singed hair, unchanged coats, not even the smell of fire","Burnt coats but living bodies","Slight burns on their hands","Their clothes turned to ashes"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 3:27",verse:"And the princes, governors, and captains, and the king’s counsellors, being gathered together, saw these men, upon whose bodies the fire had no power, nor was an hair of their head singed, neither were their coats changed, nor the smell of fire had passed on them.", insight:"Not even the smell of fire; when God delivers, He leaves no trace of the trial but the testimony."}
]},
{n:4, name:"The King's Humbling", seal:{ref:"Daniel 4:37",verse:"Now I Nebuchadnezzar praise and extol and honour the King of heaven, all whose works are truth, and his ways judgment: and those that walk in pride he is able to abase."}, facts:["Did you know Daniel 4 is written in Nebuchadnezzar's own voice? The whole chapter is the king's personal letter, his testimony of being humbled by the most High (Daniel 4:1).","Did you know Daniel's counsel to the king was practical mercy? Break off sins by righteousness, and iniquities by showing mercy to the poor (Daniel 4:27).","Did you know that when the king's reason returned, his honour and brightness returned too, and 'excellent majesty was added unto' him (Daniel 4:36)?"], questions:[
{q:"To whom did Nebuchadnezzar address his decree?", options:["To all people, nations, and languages, that dwell in all the earth","To the Chaldeans only","To the Jews in captivity","To his own sons"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:1",verse:"Nebuchadnezzar the king, unto all people, nations, and languages, that dwell in all the earth; Peace be multiplied unto you.", insight:"The proudest king on earth wrote to everybody; when God humbles a man, the testimony goes worldwide."},
{q:"Why did the king say he wrote?", options:["To show the signs and wonders that the high God had wrought toward him","To record his building projects","To announce a new law","To boast of his army"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:2",verse:"I thought it good to shew the signs and wonders that the high God hath wrought toward me.", insight:"He wrote to show what God had done to him; the humbled become the heralds."},
{q:"What did he declare about God's kingdom?", options:["His kingdom is an everlasting kingdom, and his dominion is from generation to generation","His kingdom lasts forty years","His kingdom is in Babylon","His kingdom belongs to the wise men"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:3",verse:"How great are his signs! and how mighty are his wonders! his kingdom is an everlasting kingdom, and his dominion is from generation to generation.", insight:"An everlasting kingdom; the man who thought he built forever learned what forever really means."},
{q:"What troubled the king in his palace?", options:["A dream which made him afraid","A rebellion in the provinces","A famine in the land","A plague among his servants"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:5",verse:"I saw a dream which made me afraid, and the thoughts upon my bed and the visions of my head troubled me.", insight:"At rest and flourishing, yet afraid; prosperity cannot keep out the dreams God sends."},
{q:"Who failed to interpret the dream?", options:["The magicians, the astrologers, the Chaldeans, and the soothsayers","Daniel alone","The princes of Babylon","The queen's counsellors"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:7",verse:"Then came in the magicians, the astrologers, the Chaldeans, and the soothsayers: and I told the dream before them; but they did not make known unto me the interpretation thereof.", insight:"All the wise men, and not one answer; heaven's riddles are not solved by earth's experts."},
{q:"Who came in at the last?", options:["Daniel, whose name was Belteshazzar","Arioch the captain","Ashpenaz the eunuch","The queen mother"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:8",verse:"But at the last Daniel came in before me, whose name was Belteshazzar, according to the name of my god, and in whom is the spirit of the holy gods: and before him I told the dream, saying,", insight:"At the last came Daniel; God keeps His man for the moment the wise men fail."},
{q:"What did the king call Daniel?", options:["Master of the magicians, in whom is the spirit of the holy gods","A captive of Judah","A young dreamer","A servant of the eunuchs"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:9",verse:"O Belteshazzar, master of the magicians, because I know that the spirit of the holy gods is in thee, and no secret troubleth thee, tell me the visions of my dream that I have seen, and the interpretation thereof.", insight:"Even the king saw the Spirit in him; a holy life is legible to unbelievers."},
{q:"What tree did the king see in his dream?", options:["A tree in the midst of the earth, whose height reached unto heaven","A cedar in Lebanon","An olive tree by the river","A fig tree in a garden"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:11",verse:"The tree grew, and was strong, and the height thereof reached unto heaven, and the sight thereof to the end of all the earth:", insight:"A tree reaching heaven; the dream pictured the king's own towering pride."},
{q:"What found shelter and food in the tree?", options:["The beasts had shadow under it, the fowls dwelt in its boughs, and all flesh was fed of it","Only the king's cattle","Only the birds of Babylon","No living thing"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:12",verse:"The leaves thereof were fair, and the fruit thereof much, and in it was meat for all: the beasts of the field had shadow under it, and the fowls of the heaven dwelt in the boughs thereof, and all flesh was fed of it.", insight:"All flesh was fed of it; greatness is given to shelter others, not to shade only oneself."},
{q:"Who came down from heaven in the vision?", options:["A watcher and an holy one","An army of angels","A great eagle","A whirlwind"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:13",verse:"I saw in the visions of my head upon my bed, and, behold, a watcher and an holy one came down from heaven;", insight:"A watcher came down; heaven watches, and heaven acts."},
{q:"What did the watcher cry aloud?", options:["Hew down the tree, and cut off his branches, shake off his leaves, and scatter his fruit","Water the tree and tend it","Build a wall around the tree","Cut down every tree in Babylon"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:14",verse:"He cried aloud, and said thus, Hew down the tree, and cut off his branches, shake off his leaves, and scatter his fruit: let the beasts get away from under it, and the fowls from his branches:", insight:"Hew down the tree; judgment begins with a word, and the proudest growth can fall in a day."},
{q:"What was to be left of the tree?", options:["The stump of his roots in the earth, with a band of iron and brass","Nothing at all","Only the leaves","The tallest branch"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:15",verse:"Nevertheless leave the stump of his roots in the earth, even with a band of iron and brass, in the tender grass of the field; and let it be wet with the dew of heaven, and let his portion be with the beasts in the grass of the earth:", insight:"The stump was left; judgment with mercy, a root for restoration."},
{q:"What change was decreed for the man?", options:["Let his heart be changed from man's, and let a beast's heart be given unto him","Let him be made a king forever","Let him sleep for seven days","Let him be clothed in scarlet"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:16",verse:"Let his heart be changed from man’s, and let a beast’s heart be given unto him; and let seven times pass over him.", insight:"A beast's heart for a proud heart; God gives men a taste of what pride makes them."},
{q:"Why was this decree given?", options:["To the intent that the living may know that the most High ruleth in the kingdom of men","To enrich the treasury","To frighten the Chaldeans","To honour the watchers"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:17",verse:"This matter is by the decree of the watchers, and the demand by the word of the holy ones: to the intent that the living may know that the most High ruleth in the kingdom of men, and giveth it to whomsoever he will, and setteth up over it the basest of men.", insight:"That the living may know; the lesson of the whole chapter in one sentence."},
{q:"What did Daniel say the tree was?", options:["It is thou, O king","It is the temple","It is the city of Babylon","It is the kingdom of the Medes"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:22",verse:"It is thou, O king, that art grown and become strong: for thy greatness is grown, and reacheth unto heaven, and thy dominion to the end of the earth.", insight:"It is thou, O king; the hardest sermons are the personal ones."},
{q:"What would happen to the king, according to the interpretation?", options:["They shall drive him from men, and he shall eat grass as oxen, till seven times pass over him","He would die that night","He would be exiled to Egypt","He would lose his gold"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:25",verse:"That they shall drive thee from men, and thy dwelling shall be with the beasts of the field, and they shall make thee to eat grass as oxen, and they shall wet thee with the dew of heaven, and seven times shall pass over thee, till thou know that the most High ruleth in the kingdom of men, and giveth it to whomsoever he will.", insight:"Driven from men to eat grass; pride's menu is humiliation until it learns."},
{q:"What counsel did Daniel give the king?", options:["Break off thy sins by righteousness, and thine iniquities by shewing mercy to the poor","Flee the city at once","Build a bigger palace","Sacrifice to Bel"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:27",verse:"Wherefore, O king, let my counsel be acceptable unto thee, and break off thy sins by righteousness, and thine iniquities by shewing mercy to the poor; if it may be a lengthening of thy tranquility.", insight:"Break off thy sins by righteousness; even for a tyrant, repentance had a door open."},
{q:"What boast did the king speak while walking in his palace?", options:["Is not this great Babylon, that I have built by the might of my power, and for the honour of my majesty?","Is not this the temple of the Lord?","Who is like unto me among kings?","The gods have blessed my humility"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:30",verse:"The king spake, and said, Is not this great Babylon, that I have built for the house of the kingdom by the might of my power, and for the honour of my majesty?", insight:"I have built, by my power, for my majesty; three claims of self in one sentence, and heaven answered while the word was in his mouth."},
{q:"What happened to Nebuchadnezzar the same hour?", options:["He was driven from men, ate grass as oxen, and his hair grew like eagles' feathers","He fell dead in the palace","He was taken to prison","He fled to the desert"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:33",verse:"The same hour was the thing fulfilled upon Nebuchadnezzar: and he was driven from men, and did eat grass as oxen, and his body was wet with the dew of heaven, till his hairs were grown like eagles feathers, and his nails like birds’ claws.", insight:"The same hour the word was fulfilled; God's warnings are not idle, and His timing is exact."},
{q:"What did the restored king confess at the end?", options:["He praised the King of heaven, and those that walk in pride he is able to abase","He cursed the God of Daniel","He rebuilt his idols","He blamed his counsellors"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 4:37",verse:"Now I Nebuchadnezzar praise and extol and honour the King of heaven, all whose works are truth, and his ways judgment: and those that walk in pride he is able to abase.", insight:"Those that walk in pride he is able to abase; the proudest king on earth signed his own lesson."}
]},
{n:5, name:"The Writing on the Wall", seal:{ref:"Daniel 5:27",verse:"TEKEL; Thou art weighed in the balances, and art found wanting."}, facts:["Did you know Belshazzar drank to gods of gold, silver, brass, iron, wood, and stone while using the vessels of God's own house, gods that 'see not, nor hear, nor know' (Daniel 5:4)?","Did you know Daniel refused the scarlet robe, the gold chain, and the promotion before reading a single word? 'Let thy gifts be to thyself,' he told the king (Daniel 5:17).","Did you know the writing's last word, PERES, meant 'Thy kingdom is divided, and given to the Medes and Persians' (Daniel 5:28), and that in that night the sentence was carried out and Belshazzar was slain (Daniel 5:30)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who made a great feast?", options:["Belshazzar the king","Nebuchadnezzar","Darius the Median","Cyrus"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:1",verse:"Belshazzar the king made a great feast to a thousand of his lords, and drank wine before the thousand.", insight:"Belshazzar feasted while the empire crumbled; revelry is a poor roof over a falling house."},
{q:"How many lords feasted with him?", options:["A thousand","A hundred","Ten thousand","Seventy"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:1",verse:"Belshazzar the king made a great feast to a thousand of his lords, and drank wine before the thousand.", insight:"A thousand lords drank that night; crowds do not make a party safe."},
{q:"What did Belshazzar command to be brought while he tasted the wine?", options:["The golden and silver vessels taken from the temple in Jerusalem","More wine from the cellars","The crown jewels of Babylon","Musicians and dancers"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:2",verse:"Belshazzar, whiles he tasted the wine, commanded to bring the golden and silver vessels which his father Nebuchadnezzar had taken out of the temple which was in Jerusalem; that the king, and his princes, his wives, and his concubines, might drink therein.", insight:"He reached for holy vessels to toast his gods; sacrilege is pride drinking from God's own cup."},
{q:"Who drank from the temple vessels?", options:["The king, his princes, his wives, and his concubines","Only the king alone","The priests of Bel","The captives of Judah"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:3",verse:"Then they brought the golden vessels that were taken out of the temple of the house of God which was at Jerusalem; and the king, and his princes, his wives, and his concubines, drank in them.", insight:"All of them drank; shared sin feels safe until the hand appears on the wall."},
{q:"What did they praise as they drank?", options:["The gods of gold, and of silver, of brass, of iron, of wood, and of stone","The Lord of heaven","The God of Daniel","The God of their fathers"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:4",verse:"They drank wine, and praised the gods of gold, and of silver, of brass, of iron, of wood, and of stone.", insight:"Gods of gold and stone that see not, nor hear, nor know; dead gods make bold drinkers."},
{q:"What appeared in the same hour?", options:["Fingers of a man's hand, writing on the plaister of the palace wall","A great earthquake","A pillar of fire","A host of angels"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:5",verse:"In the same hour came forth fingers of a man’s hand, and wrote over against the candlestick upon the plaister of the wall of the king’s palace: and the king saw the part of the hand that wrote.", insight:"Fingers wrote where all could see; God does not whisper when a kingdom is on trial."},
{q:"How did the king react to the writing?", options:["His countenance changed, his loins were loosed, and his knees smote together","He laughed and called for more wine","He fell asleep at the table","He drew his sword"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:6",verse:"Then the king’s countenance was changed, and his thoughts troubled him, so that the joints of his loins were loosed, and his knees smote one against another.", insight:"Knees knocking, face changed; the body confesses what the mouth will not."},
{q:"Whom did the king call to read the writing?", options:["The astrologers, the Chaldeans, and the soothsayers","The priests of Jerusalem","His army generals","The merchants of Babylon"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:7",verse:"The king cried aloud to bring in the astrologers, the Chaldeans, and the soothsayers. And the king spake, and said to the wise men of Babylon, Whosoever shall read this writing, and shew me the interpretation thereof, shall be clothed with scarlet, and have a chain of gold about his neck, and shall be the third ruler in the kingdom.", insight:"He called the same class of men who failed Nebuchadnezzar; unlearned lessons repeat themselves."},
{q:"What reward did he promise the one who could read it?", options:["Scarlet clothing, a chain of gold, and to be third ruler in the kingdom","The throne of Babylon","A thousand talents of silver","The temple vessels"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:7",verse:"The king cried aloud to bring in the astrologers, the Chaldeans, and the soothsayers. And the king spake, and said to the wise men of Babylon, Whosoever shall read this writing, and shew me the interpretation thereof, shall be clothed with scarlet, and have a chain of gold about his neck, and shall be the third ruler in the kingdom.", insight:"Scarlet and gold for an answer; dying kingdoms always bid high for what they cannot buy."},
{q:"Could the king's wise men read the writing?", options:["No, they could not read it nor make known the interpretation","Yes, at once","They read it but lied","They refused to try"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:8",verse:"Then came in all the king’s wise men: but they could not read the writing, nor make known to the king the interpretation thereof.", insight:"Not one of them could read four words; human wisdom stalls at heaven's handwriting."},
{q:"Who came into the banquet house and suggested Daniel?", options:["The queen","A Chaldean accuser","One of the lords","A servant"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:10",verse:"Now the queen, by reason of the words of the king and his lords, came into the banquet house: and the queen spake and said, O king, live for ever: let not thy thoughts trouble thee, nor let thy countenance be changed:", insight:"The queen remembered Daniel when the wise men failed; God's servant is never truly forgotten."},
{q:"What did the queen say was found in Daniel?", options:["The spirit of the holy gods, with light and understanding and wisdom","Great wealth and lands","Skill in battle","The favour of Bel"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:11",verse:"There is a man in thy kingdom, in whom is the spirit of the holy gods; and in the days of thy father light and understanding and wisdom, like the wisdom of the gods, was found in him; whom the king Nebuchadnezzar thy father, the king, I say, thy father, made master of the magicians, astrologers, Chaldeans, and soothsayers;", insight:"Light and understanding like the wisdom of the gods; a Spirit-filled life is noticed, even in a palace."},
{q:"What did the king ask Daniel when he was brought in?", options:["Art thou that Daniel, which art of the children of the captivity of Judah?","Art thou a Chaldean?","Wilt thou serve my gods?","How old art thou?"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:13",verse:"Then was Daniel brought in before the king. And the king spake and said unto Daniel, Art thou that Daniel, which art of the children of the captivity of Judah, whom the king my father brought out of Jewry?", insight:"He knew Daniel's history but not Daniel's God; knowing about a man of God is not knowing God."},
{q:"What did Daniel say about the king's gifts?", options:["Let thy gifts be to thyself, and give thy rewards to another","Give me double the reward","I will take the gold chain","Make me second ruler instead"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:17",verse:"Then Daniel answered and said before the king, Let thy gifts be to thyself, and give thy rewards to another; yet I will read the writing unto the king, and make known to him the interpretation.", insight:"He refused the payment before delivering the message; truth that cannot be bought carries weight."},
{q:"What had the most high God given to Nebuchadnezzar?", options:["A kingdom, and majesty, and glory, and honour","Only the city of Babylon","A long life alone","The temple vessels"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:18",verse:"O thou king, the most high God gave Nebuchadnezzar thy father a kingdom, and majesty, and glory, and honour:", insight:"Kingdom, majesty, glory, honour, all given; Belshazzar inherited the gifts and ignored the Giver."},
{q:"What happened when Nebuchadnezzar's heart was lifted up?", options:["He was deposed from his kingly throne, and they took his glory from him","He reigned forty more years","He conquered Egypt","He built the hanging gardens"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:20",verse:"But when his heart was lifted up, and his mind hardened in pride, he was deposed from his kingly throne, and they took his glory from him:", insight:"Lifted up in pride, cast down from the throne; the pattern was written in his own father's life."},
{q:"What charge did Daniel lay upon Belshazzar?", options:["Thou hast not humbled thine heart, though thou knewest all this","Thou hast not paid thy taxes","Thou hast not fed the poor","Thou hast not built enough"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:22",verse:"And thou his son, O Belshazzar, hast not humbled thine heart, though thou knewest all this;", insight:"He knew it all and humbled none of it; knowledge without repentance is the heaviest guilt."},
{q:"What was the writing on the wall?", options:["MENE, MENE, TEKEL, UPHARSIN","Holy, holy, holy","Babylon is fallen","Repent, O king"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:25",verse:"And this is the writing that was written, MENE, MENE, TEKEL, UPHARSIN.", insight:"Four words, and a kingdom ended; God's sentences are short and final."},
{q:"What did MENE mean?", options:["God hath numbered thy kingdom, and finished it","Thou art weighed and found wanting","Thy kingdom is divided","The Medes are at the gate"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:26",verse:"This is the interpretation of the thing: MENE; God hath numbered thy kingdom, and finished it.", insight:"Numbered and finished; every reign has a last day, and God keeps the count."},
{q:"What did TEKEL mean?", options:["Thou art weighed in the balances, and art found wanting","God hath numbered thy kingdom","Thy kingdom is given to another","Thy gods are vanity"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 5:27",verse:"TEKEL; Thou art weighed in the balances, and art found wanting.", insight:"Weighed and found wanting; the balances of heaven do not flatter kings."}
]}
]);
